abstract: >
  Structural Runtime AI (SRAI) proposes a runtime-centered
  framework for artificial intelligence. Rather than treating
  intelligence as a static trained model, SRAI views intelligence
  as a persistent runtime organization composed of Runtime
  Invariants, Runtime Assets, Runtime Organizations, Runtime
  Triggers, and Local Runtime Learning. The repository develops
  this perspective through six integrated parts: Foundations,
  Structural Operators, Structural Runtime, Runtime Intelligence,
  AI Landscape and Future Directions, and Grand Synthesis.
  Together, these parts provide a conceptual progression from
  Structural Intelligence to Persistent Runtime Intelligence,
  Runtime Representation Theory, the AI Unified Computational
  Field, and future Hybrid AI systems.

